<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17066" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτηρός</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blinded by</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτη,</span>
			<i>hurried to ruin,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				433
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				634
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					264
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>baneful, mischievous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					746
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1483
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					353
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυτιλίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.23
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				<i>bane, mischief,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					1007
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τι ἀ. ποιέωσι [οἱ
				παῖδες</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
				279
			</span></i>.—Once in Com., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτηρότατον
				κακόν</span> an 'outrageous' nuisance, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1299
			</span></i>; and so Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῶς</span> 'awfully' as a slang word, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.105K.
			</span></i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				395b
			</span></i> and c introduced only for an etym. purpose: also in later
			Prose, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				6.99
			</span></i>.</div>
